  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "development-entrance",
      "verification": "software",
      "statement": "The generic lean_develop entrance searches current project and manifest-selected mathlib source declarations as candidates, probes actual Lean constant types, accepts external complete candidates for CLI/LSP feedback, retains failures, checks buffer/source/environment/import resolution and loaded tool-code freshness before atomic save, and supports a same-process warm serve session. Feedback and save never themselves report exact-root acceptance; current generic fixture exercises failed proof -> revision -> save -> strict verification and adding a second target without research-specific constants."
    },
    {
      "id": "strict-and-continuation",
      "verification": "software",
      "statement": "Target adaptation requires a nonempty uniquely identified list with independently supplied expected_type, delegates exact roots to the retained strict verifier and evidence recheck with optional source-byte bindings, and uses existing workflow jobs for resumable start/status. Job completion or available route leaves alone does not close a root. Current generic negative cases reject extra hypotheses, missing root, transitive sorry, research axiom and model mismatch; old entry remains usable. The retained full real 15-test suite is not yet claimed passed."
    },
    {
      "id": "native-review-identity",
      "verification": "software",
      "statement": "The review adapter retains the legacy UUID protocol and also records the real collaboration.spawn_agent canonical task identity with explicit fork_turns none, exact frozen prompt, matching task name and author exclusion; only a matching native FINAL_ANSWER with full report can complete it. It rejects ordinary messages, wrong sender, missing completion and forged alternate identity fields. This is coordinator-attested transcript validation, not service-side authentication, and current unit adapter fixtures are synthetic software tests rather than evidence of a completed real review."
    },
    {
      "id": "hidden-windows-processes",
      "verification": "software",
      "statement": "Native Windows Lean/Lake, LSP, rg and actual workflow children use centralized CREATE_NO_WINDOW options while existing detached supervisor behavior and POSIX process setup are retained. Portable tests check both flag branches and a native child GetConsoleWindow result of zero; workflow native child regression passes. No Linux/WSL live run or universal no-flicker UI observation is claimed."
    }
  ],
